   "source": [
    "# Nepali Model — from-scratch training, 61036 steps\n",
    "\n",
    "Starting over with a random weight init rather than warm-starting from the\n",
    "30k-step checkpoint, since that checkpoint was trained on a corpus where\n",
    "~45% of `train.txt` was duplicate lines (train had 6,277,197 lines but only\n",
    "3,448,616 were unique). Compute cost is identical either way since\n",
    "`--init_from` never reduced `--max_steps`, so there's no downside to\n",
    "starting clean.\n",
    "\n",
    "Every bug hit while building the warm-start version is pre-patched here:\n",
    "- `git clone` failing when `repo/` already exists in the kernel\n",
    "- disk filling up during tar extraction from stale partial files\n",
    "- train/val/test overlap (deduped + reshuffled below, confirmed disjoint)\n",
    "- disk filling up *again* during the resplit write (original files are now\n",
    "  deleted progressively as they're read, instead of both copies existing\n",
    "  on disk at once)\n",
    "- the ROUGE-L-always-0.0 tokenizer bug (sanity-checked before trusting\n",
    "  `results.json`)\n",
    "- missing causal-mask verification (now a required deliverable check)\n",
    "\n",
    "Tokenizer: `nepali_tokenizer_16000.json` (16,000 vocab), used as-is.\n"
   ]
  },
