   "source": [
    "## Deduplicate + reshuffle train/val/test (fixes train/val overlap)\n",
    "\n",
    "The phase-1 `train.txt` / `val.txt` / `test.txt` overlap heavily, which is why\n",
    "tokenization above only chews through ~29 chunks (`CHUNK=5000` lines each,\n",
    "so ~145K lines) before running out of *new* content, and why val loss can't\n",
    "be trusted as a real held-out signal.\n",
    "\n",
    "This cell pools every line from all three original files, drops exact\n",
    "duplicates, shuffles once with a fixed seed, then carves out fresh disjoint\n",
    "`train.txt` / `val.txt` / `test.txt` from that pool — so train and val can\n",
    "no longer share content by construction, and train gets every unique line\n",
    "available (still capped at `MAX_TRAIN` tokens by `tokenize_to_file` below).\n",
    "\n",
    "Run this **after** the extraction above and **before** the tokenize calls below\n",
    "— it reads from `EXTRACT_DIR` and writes to `SPLIT_DIR`, which the tokenize\n",
    "calls now point at instead of the raw phase-1 files.\n",
    "\n",
    "Caveat: this only catches *exact* duplicate lines. If your corpus has\n",
    "near-duplicates (same article re-scraped with a stray whitespace/punctuation\n",
    "difference), tell me and I'll add a normalized-hash pass on top of this.\n"
   ]
  },
